# eignex-lab working notes

Benchmark lab: a Kotlin coordinator on a Mac schedules Nomad worker sessions on the Mac and on AWS spot nodes.

## Access

- Consuming repositories use `deploy/lab` and the authenticated HTTP API at `https://lab.eignex.com`.
- SSH access, host discovery and server administration belong to agents explicitly working on eignex-lab
  operations. Coordinate restarts and deployments with any other operations session.

## Storage

- The Mac's internal SSD holds hot data: the result journal, the artifact store of running jobs and caches.
- The spinning `/Volumes/Ros` disk is an archive of job data only. Never put a per-file write path for running
  jobs on it; small random writes there throttle the whole fleet.
- Ended jobs' artifacts move to the archive through `ArtifactArchiver` (`LAB_ARTIFACT_ARCHIVE`), leaving a symlink.

## Planning

- A bench's `plan` (and `describe`) makes no network requests and finishes in seconds. It selects from committed
  metadata — set files and committed corpus indexes — and declares corpus inputs by sha256; the lab fetches each
  case's bytes by hash at execution. Fix a slow or fetching planner in the consuming repository, not with lab
  workarounds.

## Deployment

- Controller (API, runner, coordinator) and worker releases deploy separately. Worker images and native launchers
  are pinned in `$LAB_DATA/nomad/queue.json`; worker-side changes take effect only after a worker rollout, which
  `deploy/worker-rollout.sh` (run by the maintenance job every five minutes) does once the commit's images are published.
- The coordinator's environment comes from `labEnvironment` in the native-services settings
  (`LAB_NOMAD_NATIVE_CONFIG`) and its installed launchd plist, not from `lab.env` alone.
- `deploy/install.sh` refuses agent or supervisor plist changes without `--restart-agents`; do not restart Nomad
  agents or the supervisor as part of an ordinary update.
- Before publishing worker images, compare every `/opt/lab` file's mode as well as its bytes with the previous image:
  `worker-entrypoint.sh` and `process_supervisor.py` must stay executable, or every container exits 126 at start.
  Start one image offline to see the entrypoint run, then switch queue targets by digest with hash-guarded edits,
  and watch the first new session start before enabling features that depend on the new worker.

## PR validation

- GitHub CI (check, native-worker, validate) is the full gate; targeted local suites during development are enough.
  Check CI before reporting a PR as green and fix failures in follow-up commits.
